      <Docs>
        <param name="builder">The builder instance.</param>
        <param name="options">The retry strategy options.</param>
        <summary>
            Adds a retry strategy limited by a retry budget to the builder. Use this method instead of
            <see cref="M:Polly.RetryResiliencePipelineBuilderExtensions.AddRetry``1(Polly.ResiliencePipelineBuilder{``0},Polly.Retry.RetryStrategyOptions{``0})" />
            in custom pipelines, because <c>AddRetry</c> can't apply <see cref="P:Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience.HttpRetryStrategyOptions.RetryBudget" /> and rejects
            options that set it.
            </summary>
        <returns>The value of <paramref name="builder" />.</returns>
        <remarks>
            The budget needs a strategy that counts every request sent through the pipeline, in addition to the retry strategy.
            This method adds both. The budget is configured by <see cref="P:Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience.HttpRetryStrategyOptions.RetryBudget" />. When it's
            <see langword="null" />, a budget with default <see cref="T:Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience.HttpRetryBudgetOptions" /> values is used, without modifying
            <paramref name="options" />. Other retry options, such as <see cref="P:Polly.Retry.RetryStrategyOptions`1.MaxRetryAttempts" />,
            are used as is. See <see cref="T:Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience.HttpRetryBudgetOptions" /> for more details.
            </remarks>
        <exception cref="T:System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations.ValidationException">Thrown when <paramref name="options" /> are invalid.</exception>
      </Docs>
